
  @X0F[@X0EU@X0F] @X0DUPLOAD A FILE
 
      @X0BWhen you upload a file to a BBS you are adding a particular file to the
      system so other users can download the file.  When you upload the
      file(s) it could immediately be made available for download, or the
      SysOp may make all uploads private to review files before posting them.
 
      When you begin an upload, you must specify the filename to upload and
      provide a description for the file before PCBoard will proceed with the
      transfer.  After the filename(s) and description(s) has been provided,
      you will see the following:
 
        @X0EUpload Drive:  341,188,608 Free Disk Space
        Upload Status: Posted Immediately
        Protocol Type: Ymodem/G BATCH
        (Ctrl-X) Aborts Transfer
 
       @X0DExamples:
 
         @X0AIf you want to upload a file called TMAL352.ZIP using Ymodem/G
         (Which is protocol G), type in the following:
 
           @X0EU TMAL352.ZIP G @X0F[@X0CENTER@X0F]
 
         @X0AYou will then be asked for a description of this file.
 
         @X0BIf you want to upload file(s) privately, use the "/" at the
         beginning of your description(s) of the file(s).
 
 
 
